  "blocks": {
    "which-service-broke-text-4": {
      "id": "which-service-broke-text-4",
      "type": "text",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "p-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Songhan Zhang, "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Aoyang Fang",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", Yifan Yang, Ruiyi Cheng, Xiaoying Tang, Pinjia He. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "arXiv preprint",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " 2510.22613, 2025."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.22613",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "arXiv"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " · "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.22613",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "PDF"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "When a fault cascades through a microservice system, the service that looks most abnormal is often a victim, not the source. DynaCausal follows the fault over a call graph rebuilt in every time window and trains the source to outrank every service it affected. On two public benchmarks it ranks the true root cause first with an average AC@1 of "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "0.63",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", 0.25 to 0.46 above the baselines."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "only": [
        "web"
      ]
    },
    "which-service-broke--scene": {
      "id": "which-service-broke--scene",
      "type": "component",
      "definitionId": "which-service-broke--scene--definition",
      "parameters": {
        "scene": "which-service-broke",
        "alt": "An online shop's services on their call graph; after a network delay, payment and ad glow the most abnormal."
      }
    },
    "the-loudest-are-victims-text-7": {
      "id": "the-loudest-are-victims-text-7",
      "type": "text",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "p-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The fault case behind the film comes from the RCAEval-RE2-OB benchmark: a network delay injected into "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "checkoutservice",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". Checkout only slows down, its latency rising from about 0.2 s to 4.8 s, while "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "paymentservice",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "adservice",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " shift their memory by about an order of magnitude. ART and Eadro score services by how abnormal they look, and both rank paymentservice (0.89 and 0.94) above checkout (0.85 and 0.92)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two more effects blur the picture. Normal fluctuations such as peak-hour traffic resemble fault signals, and what counts as normal drifts as the system evolves."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "only": [
        "web"
      ]
    },
    "the-loudest-are-victims-image-9": {
      "id": "the-loudest-are-victims-image-9",
      "type": "image",
      "assetId": "the-loudest-are-victims-asset-8",
      "alt": "Service metrics before and after the delay is injected into checkoutservice",
      "caption": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Figure 2a: metrics before and after the fault. Payment and ad memory deviate more than the root cause."
        }
      ],
      "width": 100,
      "alignment": "center",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ]
    },
    "the-loudest-are-victims-image-11": {
      "id": "the-loudest-are-victims-image-11",
      "type": "image",
      "assetId": "the-loudest-are-victims-asset-10",
      "alt": "Root cause scores of ART and Eadro for five services",
      "caption": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Figure 2b: both models score paymentservice above the true root cause, checkoutservice."
        }
      ],
      "width": 100,
      "alignment": "center",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ]
    },
    "the-loudest-are-victims-columns-12": {
